Vore Youjutsu:
Vore is a type of Combat Youjutsu that specializes on eating people. They are notably very destructive and can cripple or kill power armored targets with their magic enhanced bites.

- Most vore spells are melee range only.
- "Chomp" is a form of "hard vore", where gore and permamant body harm occurr.
- "Vore" is "soft vore", where the target is swallowed whole.
- WEAR A THICK DIAPER (or better). You will be shitting a lot after voring someone and it will come quickly.
	- Open defecation uses turns and soiling yourself unpadded also causes you to lose turns.

# Spells
Nibble: Does light Tearing damage.
	- MP Usage: None
	- Rank: G
Chomp: Takes out a limb from your target.
	Goes for limbs first. Could also go for the neck or genitals. Counts as tearing damage.
	- MP Usage: Light.
	- Rank: C
Vore: Attempt to consume the target whole.
	Will put the target in your stomach. Target must run out of STA before being digested. Will kill the target.
	Your Vore Youjutsu level will affect how much STA is taken per turn when voring. A higher level means more STA damage done to the target per turn.
	Voring people means that your food intake will shoot through the roof
	- MP Usage: Medium
	- Rank: A
Asset Flip: A combination of Vore with a little bit of Mudo.
	Takes every piece of gear that the target have and equips them to the vorer, including their gun and diaper. 
	Kills the target immediately. 
	- MP Usage: Heavy
	- Rank: Extra

# How to Neutralize
- The best tool against those that want to make you their next meal are ranged weapons. An assault rifle like the Broughton M602 can pick out an assaliant before they can Vore you.
- If you have been Vored, use a sharp melee weapon or even a laser blade like the LAC358 to cut your way through their stomach. This will destroy the vorer's stomach and allow you to escape
- Artifical body parts aren't known for tasting good.
- You can sack someone who you don't care about to the Vorer, and let them eat them. Turn stall after, letting the target poop themselves until they have a blowout in their underwear, causing subsequent diaper rash, which will damage them unless they get changed.
